data: {"type":"question.verdict","questionId":"241ab70c-a3ba-4c86-ac28-7cff0d16e0df","responseMode":"direct","headline":"셀프호스팅에서 SAML SSO 지원","condition":null,"evidence":[{"id":"e0eea171-f842-4e35-b819-28ea72f35d1f","source_type":"merged_pr","source_url":"https://github.com/supabase/supabase/pull/43386","external_ref":"#43386","heading_path":"docs(self-hosting): add SAML 2.0 SSO configuration guide > Additional context","content":"docs(self-hosting): add SAML 2.0 SSO configuration guide > Additional context\n\nThis documentation is intended to make enterprise SSO support in\nself-hosted environments clearer and production-ready, especially for\nteams deploying Supabase behind their own gateways.","audience_level":"public","valid_from":"2026-09-07T15:00:00.000Z","distance":0.510881868588956},{"id":"7c3ea22d-79c9-4c1b-b00b-5b6660a210c3","source_type":"merged_pr","source_url":"https://github.com/supabase/supabase/pull/43385","external_ref":"#43385","heading_path":"feat(self-hosting): add SAML SSO env config and open Kong routes > What kind of change does this PR introduce?","content":"feat(self-hosting): add SAML SSO env config and open Kong routes > What kind of change does this PR introduce?\n\nFeature (self-hosting infrastructure update)","audience_level":"public","valid_from":"2026-09-07T15:00:00.000Z","distance":0.5216268544654297},{"id":"2c159732-e518-4575-9b69-44d79693d8aa","source_type":"merged_pr","source_url":"https://github.com/supabase/supabase/pull/43385","external_ref":"#43385","heading_path":"feat(self-hosting): add SAML SSO env config and open Kong routes > What is the new behavior?","content":"feat(self-hosting): add SAML SSO env config and open Kong routes > What is the new behavior?\n\nThis PR:\n\n1.  Adds SAML-related environment variables to:\n    -   `docker/.env.example`\n    -   `docker-compose.yml` (Auth service section)\n2.  Exposes the following routes in `kong.yml` as open endpoints:\n    -   `/sso/saml/acs`\n    -   `/sso/saml/metadata`\n\nBoth routes are configured with CORS enabled and without authentication\nplugins, since:\n\n-   The ACS endpoint must accept POSTs from external IdPs.\n-   The metadata endpoint must be publicly retrievable by IdPs.","audience_level":"public","valid_from":"2026-09-07T15:00:00.000Z","distance":0.5527901905429626}],"latencyMs":1290}

